1
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten it up and step back to take a look.

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,660
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,280
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:42,420
That mysterious feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,780
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Go on, turn that corner.

11
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there, there's a turtle.
Surely there's a turtle.

13
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:32,960
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:34,540
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,820
Decisive Battle: Great Nature Golf

16
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,320
That's amazing, isn't it?

17
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:55,060
Renting out an entire international country golf course,
now that's really something.

18
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,580
What are you talking about?

19
00:01:56,580 --> 00:02:00,360
The fact that the prize for winning is 200,000 yen in cash is what's amazing,
isn't it?

20
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:04,780
Sure, cash beats some weird trophy any day.

21
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,020
If I had 200,000 yen...

22
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,920
It's already commanding a huge
premium before it's even released.

23
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:14,080
I could buy Saori's 1:1 scale Minia.

24
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,540
If I had 200,000 yen...

25
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,080
We could go visit Jobby,
who's in Guam for training!

26
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,060
Shock!

27
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:33,120
I've never played golf or anything.

28
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,740
We were naive, Naoko.

29
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:38,980
Don't tell me Komachi can play golf?

30
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:43,000
Actually,
I've been taking lessons for three months.

31
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,040
No way, keeping it secret is cruel!

32
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:49,280
If you want to snag a
higher-class boyfriend,

33
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:53,080
golf is a must-learn pastime, far more
than tea ceremony or flower arranging.

34
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:58,740
and a pretty decent guy teaches you hands-on,
step by step.

35
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:00,900
And he invites you on dates.

36
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:04,720
Thanks to that,
my golf skills improve rapidly.

37
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:08,740
Win this tournament and
the prize is 200,000 yen.

38
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:12,120
So the bag I've wanted
for ages is as good as mine.

39
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,740
The 200,000 yen is mine!

40
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:17,520
What are you talking about?
I'm the one who'll win!

41
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,000
What did you say?

42
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,580
I don't think any of you three will win.

43
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:26,940
Nakagawa-san

44
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:31,160
Ryo-chan's as good as the winner, isn't he?

45
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:34,800
That gorilla can actually play golf?

46
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,760
I've never heard of that.

47
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:41,680
He once played a business golf outing with
the director and the chief and the others.

48
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,780
But apparently Senpai scored
better than both of them.

49
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:49,820
On top of that, he apparently beat a pro
who makes a habit of hustling golf courses.

50
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:54,540
Yeah, his athletic ability
is truly unfathomable.

51
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,380
I didn't know that.

52
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:01,500
Plus, when money's involved,
Senpai really powers up.

53
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,160
Yeah.

54
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:04,180
That's right.

55
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,720
Are you two planning to
enter the golf competition too?

56
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,160
Of course!

57
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,920
Don't, don't.

58
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,520
That course is insanely hard.

59
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:21,120
Anyone playing it for the
first time always gives up.

60
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:25,700
So you've played at that golf course before?

61
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,360
Of course I have.

62
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,780
I'm the organizer of this competition,
remember.

63
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,300
I played there yesterday
while I was scouting it out.

64
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:35,040
Ryotsu's getting even more of an advantage,
isn't he?

65
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:38,440
Basically,
the winning prize money is already mine.

66
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:45,700
Victory is up to luck, but I'll never lose!

67
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:56,620
Group 4 is the station chief,
the chief, Nakagawa, and Reiko.

68
00:04:56,620 --> 00:05:00,780
And the final group is Komachi
Volvo and Kazushi Sanedera.

69
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,980
Does anyone have any questions?

70
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:07,520
Ryotsu: For a regular competition,
we'd leave much earlier in the morning.

71
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,080
We're taking it pretty slow, aren't we?

72
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,980
The golf course is close by.

73
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,520
And we're still within Tokyo.

74
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,080
The golf course on the riverbank?

75
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:19,020
No, it's not on the riverbank.
We're almost there.

76
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:23,320
Almost there?
Was there ever a golf course around here?

77
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:26,720
It's close, they said, but surely
it's not in the shopping arcade, right?

78
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:31,800
Here we are, we've arrived.

79
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:39,920
Where in here is the
International Country Golf Course?

80
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,640
But it's clearly written on the sign.

81
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:49,580
So "International Country"
was a person's name.

82
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:51,580
This feels pretty shady.

83
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,680
Hey, Ryotsu.

84
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:57,020
Don't tell me you embezzled
the tournament funds again and

85
00:05:57,020 --> 00:06:00,080
you didn't bring us to some weird place like this,
did you?

86
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,020
Don't be ridiculous.

87
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:04,080
You'll understand once you go inside.

88
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,800
The inside is properly kept, you know.

89
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,640
Really.

90
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,260
We've been waiting for you!

91
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:18,620
This is the owner, Mr. Kokusai.

92
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,540
Don't tell me we're
playing video game golf here?

93
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:22,340
Look.

94
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,740
There really is a course.

95
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:26,440
This is our golf course.

96
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,060
It looks pretty big.

97
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:35,480
But this course is 30 years old.

98
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:41,560
This is how things are now.

99
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:45,420
It's hardly even in the middle of town.

100
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,200
That's right, that is, this town.

101
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:54,020
Thirty years ago, there was a hill here, so we
used the natural land to build a golf course.

102
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:57,320
Tearing down a hill to build
one would be destroying nature.

103
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,780
A golf course kept in its
natural state is the best.

104
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,220
I see, so you have a philosophy.

105
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:05,100
Before long,
a railway line was going to pass through.

106
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,720
It's just the natural course of things,
so there was no help for it.

107
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:10,500
Before we knew it, a station was built.

108
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:13,460
I kept handing over my land to the government,
one piece after another.

109
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:16,560
While I just went along with
the natural flow of things,

110
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:21,860
a town naturally grew up inside the golf course.
That's how it happened.

111
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:24,760
How is that a natural golf course?

112
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:26,480
Well, don't be so stiff about it.

113
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:30,720
I've played a few rounds here myself,
and this golf course is actually quite fun.

114
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:34,980
Hole 1, 200-yard par four.

115
00:07:35,470 --> 00:07:40,200
The green is 90 yards ahead
and 110 yards to the right.

116
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,860
It's almost a course made for back alleys.

117
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:43,420
Yeah, it is.

118
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:49,260
Since it's in an alley, the fairways are super narrow too.
Looks tough.

119
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:51,880
Hazards.

120
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:55,840
Out of bounds

121
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,054
Yeah, well...

122
00:07:57,104 --> 00:08:00,540
Here, the rule is no
out-of-bounds or lost balls.

123
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:05,780
You'll play the whole course with one ball.

124
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:11,800
Losing multiple balls
is a waste of resources.

125
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,620
If you lose your ball,
you're disqualified on the spot.

126
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:17,380
That's pretty harsh.

127
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,980
Try not to hit it too far.

128
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:31,600
Nice shot! As expected of Kei-chan!
Exactly 90 yards!

129
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:33,720
Alright, my turn next!

130
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:38,800
Whoa, damn it!

131
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:43,500
It curved in nicely!

132
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:45,840
That went to a pretty good spot!

133
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,080
All's well that ends well, I guess!

134
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:54,780
My turn! If I play it safe like everyone else,
my score won't go anywhere!

135
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,420
I'm going for the one-on.

136
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,040
Owner, where's the green?

137
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:06,200
It's about between the OB Curry
and Ike-Pocha Real Estate signs.

138
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,620
What a lousy landmark.

139
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:11,860
Here goes!

140
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,760
Dammit, I missed!

141
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,840
My aim was good, though.

142
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,380
Let me show you how it's done.

143
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,580
Everyone, go to the green and watch.

144
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,140
Let's go.

145
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,300
Alright then.

146
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:36,540
I'm aiming for under that sign.

147
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:37,940
Okay.

148
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,280
Right on target.

149
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,120
It's on in one!

150
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:56,720
What do you mean, on in one? Who?

151
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:58,480
Nice!

152
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:00,400
It's an eagle chance!

153
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:02,700
He knows this course inside out.

154
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:05,260
As expected of the favorite.

155
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:06,920
What are you talking about?

156
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,960
It's only just started, you know.

157
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,380
I'm not handing over the title, no way.

158
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,220
I can't afford to lose either.

159
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:16,120
For Saori, I'll do it too!

160
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:27,420
I'm sure we came around here...

161
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,760
Sir, it's in here.

162
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,320
What?

163
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,140
In a place like this?

164
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,480
That's terrible.
You haven't eaten in three days, have you?

165
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:39,140
S-sorry.

166
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:42,940
Sir, if you're hitting, a sand wedge would be best.
What would you like to do?

167
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:44,640
I can't hit it with this, can I?

168
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,540
I give up with this.

169
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,640
Here, with this,
eat something more nutritious.

170
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,000
Th-thank you very much.

171
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,760
Oh no, my ball!

172
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,660
I'm sorry, but you're disqualified.

173
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,040
Ganka-ri.

174
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:19,440
Over the road I'll have to hit a high ball.

175
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:23,900
Nice shot!

176
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:37,680
Sir, if you don't go after it,
you'll be disqualified.

177
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:41,260
No way. Since it's a lost ball, I give up.

178
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:44,400
Wah! Don't stare at me like that!

179
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:49,720
That's enough.

180
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,440
Here I go!

181
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:57,000
All the people who don't care about
money are dropping out one by one.

182
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,500
This makes me even more of an advantage,
doesn't it.

183
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:30,120
Going aggressive here like
this is the safest bet, so

184
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:33,260
When there's money on the line,
you really get brainy, don't you.

185
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:40,940
Caddie, where's my ball?

186
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,740
It's under that car.

187
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,200
Just a little more.

188
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,160
No good, I can't get it out.

189
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,920
Volvo... so you're finally giving up?

190
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:59,040
You don't need to worry about that.

191
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,940
W-what are you planning to do?

192
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:05,960
Everyone, get back, it's dangerous!

193
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,360
D-damn you, you idiot!

194
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,040
On the third stroke,

195
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:20,060
It's out!

196
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,160
Alright, par on the fourth stroke.

197
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:32,580
This isn't golf anymore.

198
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,520
Don't hit it somewhere dangerous! Run!

199
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:40,300
Oi!

200
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:45,020
Who the hell is blasting balls into our place?!
Come out!

201
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,340
It's you!

202
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:47,640
What? No, it wasn't me!

203
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:58,220
Are we going to hit over there too?

204
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:00,280
If you don't hit, you're disqualified.

205
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:03,360
Looks like Komachi's finished here too.

206
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:06,940
What? You're joking. Hold on a second.

207
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:08,220
Komachi!

208
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:10,760
What's Komachi planning to do?

209
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,880
What's this? It's a golf ball.

210
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,480
What? What is it?

211
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,280
What was that?

212
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,520
What was that just now?

213
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:39,640
No idea.

214
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:44,840
Are you okay, Komachi?

215
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:47,320
I somehow managed to get out.

216
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:50,120
Even as a woman, to go this far...

217
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:53,300
Komachi might be the toughest rival.

218
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,000
A 600-yard long hole

219
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:02,900
Ryotsu and Kodasaka

220
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:06,160
We have no choice but
to go for an eagle here.

221
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,980
Ree-ree

222
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:15,440
Oh no, it went into the bathhouse!

223
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,940
And there are men in there too!

224
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:19,440
Damn, that's too bad.

225
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,820
Alright, I'm going straight for it.

226
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:23,680
Hey.

227
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:30,960
Oh no, now it's the women's bath!
Don't go deliberately aiming for it.

228
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:37,400
Bolbo's weak to women's nudes,
so that's the end of it.

229
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,660
You're not going to win.

230
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,540
It's all old men,
not the least bit exciting.

231
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,880
If I was going to hit one,
I should've aimed for the women's bath.

232
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,220
Anyway, it's all old ladies.

233
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:57,300
Isn't it!

234
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:16,080
Looks like there was a young customer.

235
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,060
I'm a little jealous.

236
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:23,480
Kankichi Ryotsu, your second shot is next.

237
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:28,620
Lucky!

238
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:31,980
This is how you conquer
a straight long hole.

239
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:36,960
Alright!

240
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:41,060
There!

241
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:44,400
Hehehe.
Now it's a straight shot to the green.

242
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,640
Ugh, what a lucky bastard.

243
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,440
At this rate, the gap just keeps widening.

244
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:51,360
Naoko, hey.

245
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:52,780
Yeah, yeah.

246
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:55,740
Got it. If you win, you're treating me.

247
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,518
Whoa, damn it.

248
00:16:59,568 --> 00:17:02,440
I didn't figure it would stop this quickly.

249
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:07,620
Lucky again?

250
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:16,500
What? H-hey, stop right there!

251
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,360
That's the end of you too, Ryo-san.

252
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:27,160
You're a persistent one, aren't you?
How about this?

253
00:17:30,980 --> 00:17:33,320
Damn it, it curved again!

254
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,900
Here I go!

255
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,900
Hey! Get back here!

256
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:46,720
Ah, Naoko!

257
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:47,920
No way!

258
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:49,200
You played dirty, you bastard!

259
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,960
No matter what you do, the 200,000 is mine!

260
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:03,960
If that's how you want it,
I've got plenty of dirty tricks too!

261
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,500
Taxi!

262
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:13,160
Formidable... a stronghold, a naval base.

263
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:16,480
W-what is this?! Who are you people?!

264
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:18,391
Yes, Sakonji.

265
00:18:18,441 --> 00:18:22,360
Firing into a room at Saori's house,
just like yours, was your bad luck.

266
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:26,160
If you try to shoot,
you'll end up hurting Saori.

267
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:29,860
Only by overcoming trials is there victory!

268
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:35,185
No good.

269
00:18:35,235 --> 00:18:38,920
I can't bring myself to hurt Saori.

270
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:41,820
One person's out.

271
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:48,320
W-what is this hole?

272
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:49,724
Hole nine.

273
00:18:49,774 --> 00:18:56,340
The final stage is a 350-yard par 4 using the garden of Ōjinushi,
a lover of animals.

274
00:18:56,680 --> 00:19:01,460
It's a difficult course where most
players take risks on this ninth hole.

275
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:04,340
The only players left are the senior ones

276
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,360
Alright, I have the honor.

277
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:07,592
Damn it,

278
00:19:07,642 --> 00:19:11,620
It really hurt that I blew
all my savings on the last hole.

279
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:13,740
Anyway, I'll just hit it far here

280
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:16,240
and make sure we don't
run into those wild beasts.

281
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,100
Nice shot!

282
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,860
Wow! It's going over 300 yards!

283
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:33,160
Looks like you're giving up now

284
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:34,740
No, not yet.

285
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:39,580
Are you planning to chase the helicopter?

286
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,560
What relentless determination.

287
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,980
We're in the middle of a pack of tigers.

288
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:50,260
You'd better withdraw.

289
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:53,560
We've come this far, we can't just give up.

290
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:55,700
I'm going to win, no matter what.

291
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:58,660
This tough hole is too much for a woman.

292
00:19:58,660 --> 00:19:59,680
Here goes.

293
00:20:01,260 --> 00:20:03,910
Damn it,

294
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:06,660
I hooked it.

295
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:12,080
Of all places, it landed right there.

296
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:14,840
This is our chance.

297
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,160
Don't you dare wake up now.

298
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:24,860
Looks like it's hunting time now.

299
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:41,820
It's a chance.

300
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:49,040
After all, it's a chance.

301
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:10,940
This is where the senpai
really shows his true worth.

302
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:19,840
We finally took down those beasts,
and now we're stuck in the water hazard?

303
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:24,600
We're two strokes ahead; if we get out of this spot,
we're golden.

304
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:45,520
Nooooooooooooooooooooo!

305
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,120
Ahead of you.

306
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:50,360
Yes!

307
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:52,320
One over, and that's the hole.

308
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,100
Damn it!

309
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:55,100
That 200,000 yen is mine.

310
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,840
Ryo-chan's next shot is his fourth stroke.

311
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:59,120
Unless he sinks this,
there's no way he wins.

312
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:00,600
Even Ryotsu...

313
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,820
There's no way he chips in from there.

314
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:03,720
No, no.

315
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:05,680
When money's involved, the senpai will...

316
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:07,920
pull off a miracle or anything else.

317
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,260
There's only one place to aim for.

318
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,760
[Unclear]

319
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,160
Brrrrr!

320
00:22:21,300 --> 00:22:24,040
Ugh, hehehe.

321
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:28,800
Are you some kind of
pro golfer or something?!

322
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:34,220
Did it go in?!

323
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,800
Yes! It's a playoff!

324
00:22:39,140 --> 00:22:40,760
Well, I wouldn't be so sure about that.

325
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:56,160
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

326
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:02,640
Yay! We're the champions!

327
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,520
No way!

328
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:07,220
I can't believe you'd
already tamed it up to ten.

329
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:11,440
Looks like that 200,000 yen is mine now.

330
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:18,600
Somebody help me!

331
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:21,880
Weren't you buttering them up?

332
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,860
Looks like they've been treating us.

333
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:26,700
Hey! That 200,000 yen is mine, you hear?

334
00:23:27,020 --> 00:23:28,180
Keep it!

335
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:35,200
Guess it always ends up like this.

336
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:37,560
By the way, where did Bolb go?

337
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:40,320
Now that you mention it, he went off
chasing the helicopter and never came back.

338
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:45,500
872.

339
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:49,480
Damn, I never thought we'd
end up all the way in Fukushima.

340
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:53,520
Hey! Huh? It's 873!

341
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:57,620
When are we ever going to finish this hole?!

342
00:24:01,180 --> 00:24:05,540
Kicking the alarm clock, my pinky goes
"ow ow ow"

343
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:13,920
Quickly draw on my brows,
then dash, dash, dash to the station

344
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:19,560
Packed train, a nap on Dad's back

345
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:25,860
Hard work again this week,
unreasonable demands are only natural

346
00:24:27,100 --> 00:24:33,360
Holding a baguette and looking so composed,
but it's beef bowl with extra soupy sauce

347
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:40,260
Irritation from endless overtime,
cleared up neatly by getting irritated

348
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:50,040
Every day is no problem,
once I've passed through a hot shower

349
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:56,580
Every day is no problem,
recharging my energy on a sleep pillow

350
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:06,240
Every day is no problem,
I love a girl like me

351
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:09,320
Every day is no brain

352
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:13,040
Hearts flying on a Monday

353
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:22,960
What? Nakagawa wants to
turn his life into a system?

354
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:23,960
Don't make me laugh

355
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,340
Using nothing but cards

356
00:25:25,340 --> 00:25:28,200
What can you do,
someone who's never even seen cash?

357
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:29,120
Alright!

358
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,840
I'll show you what a
real contract life is like

359
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,340
Thoroughly

360
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:34,100
Next time

361
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:37,240
Transform into a man of the people,
Nakagawa, good luck with that

